{
  "abstract": "Over half of the known rational almost Diophantine septuples ($20/21$ square pairs) contain a two-sided regular quintuple, yet generic quintuple fibres force the sixth entry onto curves of genus at least $9$. We invert this elimination by parameterizing the sub-quadruple in $(r,\\lambda,S_{ab})$, where the regular fifths become linear in the trace $S_{ab}$ and all three remaining conditions complete the square in $S_{ab}$. Vanishing of their discriminants cuts out two families of sextuple and $19/21$ septuple surfaces: the Branch-1 surface $E_{Br1}$ and the twin-fifth surfaces $E_{F1}, E_{F3}$. A chord census yields $2,304$ rational sextuples ($408$ positive) and a new rational almost septuple $S_7^{(20/21)}$ of relation type $(5,2)$. Factoring the four-variable regular relation on the fifths defines $S_{4,2}$, whose Branch-1 specialization is a smooth genus-three curve $H$, proving finiteness by Faltings' theorem and unramified two-cover descent. In $(r,\\mu,z)$ and Lorentz $(r,u,v,\\theta)$ coordinates, we establish the One-$R_5$ Dual Brahmagupta blow-up $P_{blowup}=0$ and Two-Conic surface $P_{surf}=0$ covering $N_{core}=0$ ($4:1$), classify sub-regular and collision curves (including $F_{12}=0$ and a $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{133})$ almost septuple), and prove a $2$-adic lock on $E_B$ and rank-zero descent on $E_{16}$. Finally, we establish $3$-torsion Master Syzygies closing $C_{triad}$ and $H=1/3$, paired/antipodal source closures, the plane cubic model $C_T$, the Monomial Fifth Law, and the Bi-Euler, Chebyshev, and Osculating $S_7^{osc}(R,\\kappa)$ towers on the symplectic Euler plane $V_{Euler}$. No rational Diophantine septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "This revision implements all four recommendations from the Version 24 acceptance review and adds Theorem 20(73)-(75) (Item 30 in THEOREMS_AND_PROOFS.md, verified in exp71_chebyshev_pi_completed_square_and_reflection_duality.py and verify_paper.py): (1) Corrected the slope identity to kap = d_-/k where k = (Y_0 - 1)/(X_0 - 1) = (X_{d_-}(w_0) - 1)/(X_b(w_0) - 1) in Section 9, Item 29, and exp70; cited P. Gibbs (arXiv:math/9903035, 1999) on generalised Stern-Brocot trees from regular quadruples and corrected Arkin-Hoggatt-Bergum to Arkin-Hoggatt-Strauss; confined the degree-16 irreducibility statement for 1 + g_0*e_+ in Q[k] to the certified fiber (r,t) = (2,4); and stated the automatic square counts 10N+3, 12N+1, 12N+2, 12N+3, 12N+4 on the open non-degenerate locus where entries are distinct and nonzero; (2) Added Theorem 20(73): the Universal Chebyshev Scalar Pi = R(w_0, w_1) = R*u_0 + X_0*Y_0, the Universal Completed-Square Identity (P*Pi^2 - R^2)^2*(1 + g_0*e_+) == (2*R*Pi*S_{b,d_-} + (R+1)*(3*R-1)*Pi^2 + R^2)^2 - 4*R*(R+1)*Pi^2*((R+1)*Pi^2 - R), and Fricke descent (kap -> P/kap) of 1 + g_0*e_+ to a degree-8 polynomial in tau_kap = kap + P/kap (irreducible of degree 8, genus 3, on (r,t) = (2,4)); (3) Added Theorem 20(74): closed-form S = r^2 formulas on 5*r^2 - 1 = rho^2 and Klein-four (V_4 = <r -> -r, rho -> -rho>) descent of 1 + g_0(q)*e_+(q) to N_{38}(S)/D_{19}(S)^2 with N_{38}(S) irreducible of degree 38 in Q[S] and degree 76 in Q[r]; and (4) Added Theorem 20(75): Reflection Duality I_{C_0}(tau_kap) = -(C_0*tau_kap + 4*R^2)/(C_0 + tau_kap) swapping u_1 <-> u_{-1}, the J_R involution swapping c^*_- <-> c^*_+, the completed-square law for 1 + c^*_-*c^*_+, and Z = sig_kap^2 descent of the 3 remaining gates of S_7^{osc}(R, kap) to rational functions G_-(R, Z), G_+(R, Z), G_{-+}(R, Z) of degrees 10, 10, 18 with G_+(R, Z) == G_-(-R, Z).",
